               </text>
            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent inpatient treatment of your patient, a 66-year-old male, admitted on 22/06/2002 due to acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemic respiratory failure, chest X-ray showing hyperinflation without consolidation, and ECG to exclude cardiac cause. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. Treatment consisted of controlled oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and close monitoring of vital signs and oxygen saturation. The patient responded well to therapy with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged home in stable condition on 23/06/2002. We recommend continuation of optimised inhaler therapy and close follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact us with any questions.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
